            "review_title": "Review at Nha Hang Vua Hai San",
            "review_text": "Rishi K\n4 contributions\n0\nTerrible Experience - Avoid This Restaurant!\nAug 2024 • Family\nIf you're looking for a place where customers are completely disrespected, then this is the restaurant for you. We were seated and politely asked if we could move closer to the water, which was initially arranged. Then the floor manager came over to explain the lobster's daily price, which was 3,600,000 VND per kilo. He showed the price on his calculator and said that further information could be found on the menu, and for certain fish, we would need to ask for the price. So far, so good.\n\nHowever, we decided not to order lobster and chose other dishes instead from the menucard. That’s when everything changed. When we wanted to order drinks, the same man informed us that since we didn’t order lobster, the price of the drinks had doubled, with a minimum price of 100,000 VND. As if that wasn't ridiculous enough, we were also told that we could no longer sit by the water and had to move further back because we didn’t order lobster. These were 'the rules.'\n\nWhen I pointed out that it was rude not to inform us of these rules when we were seated, the floor manager showed no understanding whatsoever. He didn’t apologize and simply said that the owner makes the rules and there’s nothing he could do about it. This was odd since he appeared to be the floor manager.\n\nThe final straw was when, as we were leaving, another guest approached us and asked what had happened. He mentioned that he had been given a daily price of 2,000,000 VND per kg for the same lobster and that he overheard the floor manager saying something in Vietnamese that didn’t sit well with him. The guest apologized on behalf of the staff and assured us that not all Vietnamese people are like this.\n\nOverall, this restaurant has no respect for its customers. Rude staff, shady pricing practices, and zero customer service. I strongly advise everyone to avoid eating here.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nAtmosphere\nWritten August 13, 2024",
